# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# You usually do NOT need this file.
#
# The simplest setup is to drop your service-account JSON, exactly as Google
# gave it to you, at:
#
#     secrets/vertex-sa.json
#
# and run `npm run check`. The tool finds it on its own. secrets/ is gitignored.
#
# Everything below is for the cases where you would rather not keep the key
# inside the project. Pick ONE. Nothing here is ever printed in full.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1) Service-account JSON key file somewhere else on disk.
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/path/to/vertex-sa.json

# 1b) Same thing, but inline (useful in CI where you only have env vars):
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type":"service_account","project_id":"...","private_key":"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n..."}

# 2) An already-minted OAuth2 token, e.g. `gcloud auth print-access-token`.
# GOOGLE_ACCESS_TOKEN=ya29....

# 3) A Vertex AI express-mode API key.
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project + region
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed if the key file has no project_id, or to override it.
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=my-project-id

# Preferred region. me-west1 is Tel Aviv:
#   https://me-west1-aiplatform.googleapis.com
# VERTEX_REGION=me-west1
